      "full_page": "NOTE. What might well be termed: \"A prize-essay indeed\", especially if taken in connection with her superhuman courage and perfect resignation in the sarcoma cancer that started shortly after she had written the following and held her captive till Dec. 13, 1947. Kathleen Stiverson, about to grad- uate in the eighth grade, aged 12, she wrote as follows: (her sturdy father and pius mother re- spectively from Holland and Ireland as did many others learn patience from her and perfect re- signation).",
