      "full_page": "NOTE Little Cathleen (R.I.P.) went to the Little Flower School, St. Therese of Royal Oak, Michigan. Her teacher, Sister M. marked her \"Excellent\" and then adds: \"And our joy Kathleen. Nothing is hard to love and Fiat.\" Less than a year following Kathleen was stricken with sarcomic cancer, which the doctors figured would take her inside of four months. She battled with it for over a year and half without a single complaint. Rev. Father Coughlin refered to her on occasion of her funeral as: \"A second \"Little Flower.\"",
